## Summary

**Root cause:** The mutation-survival implementation added a new required field `mutation_survival: f64` to `FileRisk`, but 24 existing `FileRisk { ... }` initializers in test code had not been updated — compiler error E0063.

**Fixes:**
1. Added `mutation_survival: 0.0` to every existing FileRisk initializer across:
   • `src/commands_risk.rs` (24 sites)
   • `src/commands_risk_snapshots.rs` (6 sites)
   • `src/commands_risk_emerging.rs` (11 sites)
   • `src/commands_risk_report.rs` (13 sites — the one already having the field was left untouched)
2. Added the task-required unit tests for `load_mutation_survival in src/commands_risk.rs`:
   • `test_load_mutation_survival_well_formed` — validates parsing, clamping to [0,1], skipping 0.0/non-numeric entries
   • `test_load_mutation_survival_malformed_and_missing` — fail-soft on malformed JSON, empty file, and absent file

**Verification (all passed):**
• `cargo fmt -- --check` ✓
• `cargo build` ✓
• `cargo test` — 4345 passed, 0 failed (bin) + 88 passed (lib + integration) ✓
• `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` ✓

The implementation itself (loader, 0.10-weight fold into score, `▲mut-surv` signal, `mut %` display in report, fail-soft behavior when `.arc/mutants_per_file.json` is absent) was already in place and remains unchanged — users without the artifact see identical risk scores and reports.
